<!--Post: 6285--><!--Time: 1107658570-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6285"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bestbud<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bestbud<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 6:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Some interesting words &#40;typesetting and railroad ties&#41; and paragraphs in the Article: <BR> <BR>Assembled in the similar pursuits of congeniality, the tavern customers, regardless of ideology, fell into a receptive state. In this way, a middle-aged future owner of the bar, Dudley, found himself in proximity to wild youth. &#34;Dudley started coming into the bar during the day. He was a clinical alcoholic who had stayed dry. He&#39;d come in there and do a couple of business deals over the phone—selling typesetting equipment. Then he fell off the wagon.&#34;  <BR> <BR>John Byers ran A Blackout from 1975 to 1978, taking it over from Dudley. According to Byers, Dudley ran a loose ship, sleeping on the bar, giving his dog an inviolable corner, and acting very much annoyed if he were called upon to furnish potations.  <BR> <BR>Byers had definite ideas on tavern management, partly defined through his experiences in the bar when McNabb owned it. &#34;I wanted to bring it back to life. I put seashells everywhere and made it a seaside bar.&#34;  <BR> <BR>He also put wood chips and railroad ties behind the building, as well as a tall fence, so that his patrons could take in the out-of-doors in good weather with some privacy. The entertainment was a jukebox with hard-to-find records whose message was fiercely anti-disco. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ku.edu/heritage/beats/ablackout.html" target=_top>http://www.ku.edu/heritage/beats/ablackout.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6285-->
<!--Post: 6294--><!--Time: 1107662271-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6294"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 7:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I know from my own mistakes that your post will have to come down because it was copied...however, I love that site and have wondered about Byers for a couple of months. Haven&#39;t been able to track him past &#39;78.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6294-->
<!--Post: 6295--><!--Time: 1107662582-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6295"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bestbud<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bestbud<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 8:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh!  Sorry...Didn&#39;t know I wasn&#39;t supposed to copy and paste info.  Thanks for the heads up! ;&#41; <BR> <BR>Did you check out the White Van with the &#34;Unidentifed&#34; Logo? Hmmmm.... <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6295-->
<!--Post: 6297--><!--Time: 1107663205-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6297"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 8:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yep - Moody&#39;s Skidrow Beanery &#40;steaming coffee mug&#41; is the logo. Google Moody&#39;s - don&#39;t know if its relevant - but it is interesting nonetheless.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6297-->
<!--Post: 6301--><!--Time: 1107664655-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6301"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 8:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is a John Byers in northwest Wichita, no idea if it is the same one. He lives around the area of 53rd north and Seneca. This is very close to the last drop off area.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?ed=PaluM.p_0TrI8IJHI60sl0VlnPW6xbuosw--&amp;csz=WICHITA%2BKS%2B67204&amp;country=us&amp;cat=&amp;trf=0" target=_top>http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?ed=PaluM.p_0TrI8 IJHI60sl0VlnPW6xbuosw--&amp;csz=WICHITA&#43;KS&#43;67204&amp;count ry=us&amp;cat=&amp;trf=0</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6301-->
<!--Post: 6302--><!--Time: 1107665012-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6302"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 8:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Fwiw, PJ O&#39;Connor mentions in his book that he had a harmonica playing friend who worked at Coleman. They played music together at A Blackout. His name was Bill. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6302-->
<!--Post: 6314--><!--Time: 1107674492-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6314"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 11:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Don&#39;t overlook Dudley. I wonder where he landed?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6314-->
<!--Post: 6327--><!--Time: 1107700540-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6327"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 6:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From &#34;Tales From A Blackout&#34;: <BR> <BR>&#34;&#39;During the day it was open forum, longhairs sitting next to guys with ties. Then at night it was pretty much freaks.&#39; In this way, a middle-aged future owner of the bar, Dudley, found himself inproximity to wild youth.&#34; <BR> <BR>Middle-aged? Too old?  <BR> <BR>Can anyone tell me who was &#34;The Irishman&#34;? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6327-->
<!--Post: 6386--><!--Time: 1107745657-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6386"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 7:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From the link in the first post this caught my eye: <BR> <BR>&#34;Ina&#39;s had been a rough place. She had a nightstick carved like a dildo and she would use it on anyone that got out of line.&#34; <BR> <BR>Was it not stated that a possible victim received a drawing involving a nightstick?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6386-->
<!--Post: 6388--><!--Time: 1107749332-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6388"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 8:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry, I found it, posted by Johno on 12/20/04: <BR>&#34;It is of further interest to note that in a drawing he sent to would-be victim Anna Williams he shows what investigators and others who have seen it, what is described as a billy club or police baton being inserted into a body cavity.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6388-->
